                <head>No. 80<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>On August 23 Prime Minister Attlee wrote to President Truman concerning the
                    situation in Iran following the failure of the Stokes Mission. After reviewing
                    the progress of the talks, thanking the President for the assistance rendered by
                    Harriman and Levy, and expressing agreement with the United States that there
                    was danger of Iran falling under Communist domination, Attlee urged the
                    President to state that the United States Government fully supported the British
                    stand, that it regarded the breakdown in the <pb facs="0181" n="155"
                        xml:id="pg155"/> talks as solely the fault of the Iranian Government, and
                    that the disaster which now threatened Iran was due only to the policy of that
                    government. (A copy of this message is in file 888.2553/10–1051.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
